>
  <article class="max-w-[990px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight mb-4" style="color: var(--text-primary);">IBPS PO 2026 — Photo, Signature, Thumb Impression & Declaration Guide</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">

      <p>IBPS PO requires four separate uploads during registration — more than any other major exam: a photo, a signature, a left thumb impression, and a handwritten declaration. Missing the spec on any one of them can hold up your application. Here's the exact requirement for each, and how to prepare them.</p>

      <div class="toc">
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#photo">Photo</a></li>
          <li><a href="#signature">Signature</a></li>
          <li><a href="#thumb">Left Thumb Impression</a></li>
          <li><a href="#declaration">Handwritten Declaration</a></li>
          <li><a href="#step-by-step">Step-by-Step Preparation</a></li>
          <li><a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 id="photo">Photo</h2>

      <p><strong>200×230 pixels</strong>, <a href="/compress/to-50kb">20–50KB</a>, JPEG/JPG. A recent colour passport-style photo with a light or white background. No selfies — use a DSLR or professional photo. Live photo capture is also required during registration, separate from this scanned upload.</p>

      <h2 id="signature">Signature</h2>

      <p><strong>140×60 pixels</strong>, <a href="/compress/to-20kb">10–20KB</a>, JPEG/JPG. Black ink on white paper, running handwriting — not capital letters. This signature must match all your future exam documents, so sign it the way you always sign.</p>

      <h2 id="thumb">Left Thumb Impression</h2>

      <p><strong>240×240 pixels</strong>, <a href="/compress/to-50kb">20–50KB</a>, JPEG/JPG. Use a blue or black ink pad on white paper. The impression must be clear and not smudged — a light or partial print is a common cause of rejection. Visually handicapped (VH) candidates may submit a written declaration instead of a thumb impression.</p>

      <h2 id="declaration">Handwritten Declaration</h2>

      <p><strong>800×400 pixels</strong> (10cm × 5cm at 200 DPI), <a href="/compress/to-100kb">50–100KB</a>, JPEG/JPG. Must be written in English, in the candidate's own handwriting, not in capital letters, certifying that all information provided is accurate. The declaration text may be typed only if the candidate is unable to write.</p>

      <h2 id="step-by-step">Step-by-Step Preparation</h2>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Resize</strong> your photo to 200×230px using the <a href="/resize/for-ibps">IBPS resize tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Compress</strong> the photo to 20–50KB using the <a href="/compress/for-ibps">IBPS compress tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Compress your signature</strong> to 10–20KB using the <a href="/compress/signature">signature compress tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Compress the thumb impression</strong> to 20–50KB using the <a href="/compress/to-50kb">50KB compress tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Compress the declaration</strong> to 50–100KB using the <a href="/compress/to-100kb">100KB compress tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Convert to JPEG</strong> if any file is PNG or HEIC, using the <a href="/convert/png-to-jpg">PNG to JPG converter</a>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Signature written in capital letters instead of running handwriting</li>
        <li>Blurry or smudged thumb impression</li>
        <li>Declaration written by someone other than the candidate</li>
        <li>Wrong file sizes for one or more of the four uploads</li>
        <li>Reusing an old photo instead of a recent one</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-[14px]">Specifications listed here are based on publicly available information as of 2026. Always verify the current requirements from the official exam notification before uploading.</p>

    </div>
